# PHP build dependencies (Homebrew formula names), one or more per line; '#'
# comments and blank lines ignored. Names differ from packages.dnf/packages.apt
# (Homebrew vs. rpm/deb naming) but the covered capabilities are meant to match,
# minus two with no macOS equivalent: PHP-FPM's systemd notify (systemd-devel —
# launchd has no analogue) and gd's XPM support (no Homebrew libXpm/X11
# formula this build wires up). AVIF is not a third gap: Homebrew's `gd`
# formula depends on `libavif` unconditionally (confirmed via `brew info
# --json gd`; its shipped gdlib.pc links `-lavif`), so AVIF support rides in
# for free once `gd` is installed below. Installs go through
# pkg_install_optional, which warns on a missing formula instead of failing;
# the smoke gate in scripts/darwin/mise-install.sh is what catches a dropped
# capability — pair list changes with gate changes.
#
# Cross-checked against the actual build logic of the pinned vfox-php plugin
# (mise.toml's [tool_alias]: vfox:jdx/vfox-php, a fork of mise-plugins/vfox-php
# confirmed byte-identical as of 2026-07) — its hooks/post_install.lua wires
# PKG_CONFIG_PATH from a hardcoded "required" list on darwin, and separately
# appends a --with-X flag for each "optional" formula it finds installed. See
# scripts/darwin/mise-install.sh's header for what that means for this list and
# what is still unverified.

# Build toolchain (buildconf + configure need these; the plugin PATH-only-wires
# bison/re2c, so pkg_install_optional's own PATH-driven install is what makes
# them reachable at all)
autoconf automake libtool pkg-config bison re2c
# Core compile deps the plugin wires into PKG_CONFIG_PATH unconditionally
# (macOS ships none of these as a linkable, pkg-config-discoverable dev tree)
libxml2 openssl@3 zlib krb5 libedit curl
# pdo_sqlite, sqlite3 — PHP 8.4+ dropped its bundled SQLite copy, so a linkable
# sqlite3 is mandatory on every platform now, not just this one; also one of
# the plugin's PKG_CONFIG_PATH-wired formulas
sqlite
# mbstring
oniguruma
# intl (ICU)
icu4c
# zip — the plugin does NOT auto-add --with-zip the way it does --with-sodium/
# --with-bz2/--with-pdo-pgsql/--with-external-gd (see those entries below), so
# scripts/darwin/mise-install.sh states the flag explicitly; libzip only needs
# to be findable via pkg-config for that to work
libzip
# gd itself — REQUIRED, and easy to miss: --with-external-gd (forced,
# unconditionally, in scripts/darwin/mise-install.sh) makes php-src's
# configure run PKG_CHECK_MODULES([GDLIB], [gdlib >= 2.1.0]), and that .pc
# file ships with the `gd` formula, not with any of its dependencies below —
# installing only those leaves gdlib.pc absent and configure fails outright.
# Confirmed via `brew info --json gd`: it is its own formula (dependencies
# fontconfig, freetype, jpeg-turbo, libavif, libpng, libtiff, webp), not a
# meta-package for them.
gd
# freetype/libpng/webp — `gd`'s own dependencies (Homebrew installs them
# automatically once gd, above, is installed); listed here too for
# visibility, though --with-freetype/--with-png/--with-webp (which the
# plugin's own build logic would auto-add for these) apply only to PHP's
# BUNDLED gd build — php-src's ext/gd/config.m4 documents them "only for
# bundled libgd", and this build forces --with-external-gd, so those three
# flags are inert here. What actually matters is that `gd`'s own compiled
# library already links freetype/libpng/webp (and libavif — see the header
# above), which --with-external-gd picks up as-is
freetype libpng webp
# jpeg — NOT an alias for jpeg-turbo, which `gd` depends on above (Homebrew
# ships them as two separate, independently-versioned formulas; `jpeg`'s own
# aliases are libjpeg/libjpg). The plugin's build logic would auto-add
# --with-jpeg for this formula, but — same as freetype/libpng/webp above —
# that flag is inert under the forced --with-external-gd; jpeg-turbo (gd's
# actual, load-bearing JPEG dependency) installs regardless, pulled in
# transitively by gd. Kept here mainly so a future reader isn't left
# wondering why two differently-named jpeg formulas exist side by side
jpeg
# sodium — the plugin's own optional_packages logic auto-adds --with-sodium
# when this resolves; harmless either way, since ext/sodium's config.m4 is
# PKG_CHECK_MODULES-only (no directory argument) and libsodium isn't
# keg-only, so the default pkg-config search finds it regardless
libsodium
# readline — the plugin's own optional_packages logic auto-adds a
# path-qualified --with-readline=$(brew --prefix readline), and that path IS
# needed: readline is keg-only and ext/readline's config.m4 does a raw
# header-path search with no pkg-config fallback (--with-libedit, the
# alternative that path exists for, is never selected here)
readline
# bz2 — scripts/darwin/mise-install.sh states --with-bz2=$(brew --prefix
# bzip2) explicitly rather than relying on the plugin's own auto-add: bzip2
# is keg-only, ext/bz2's config.m4 has no pkg-config fallback at all, and
# PHP_EXTRA_CONFIGURE_OPTIONS is appended after the plugin's own configure
# string — restating the flag WITHOUT a path there would silently override
# the plugin's already-correct one back to a bare "yes", the exact failure a
# real build caught ("bzlib.h not found")
bzip2
# pdo_pgsql — same reasoning and same fix as bz2 above: libpq is keg-only,
# ext/pdo_pgsql's config.m4 falls back to a raw pg_config/header search with
# no usable pkg-config path (libpq isn't in the plugin's PKG_CONFIG_PATH-wired
# formula list, only its path-qualified-flag one), and
# scripts/darwin/mise-install.sh states --with-pdo-pgsql=$(brew --prefix
# libpq) explicitly for the same override-safety reason
libpq
# PECL imagick (runtime + headers)
imagemagick
# PECL memcached
libmemcached
